<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to auction 7-yr bonds of HUF 5bln on May 8.</title>
<headline>Hungary to auction 7-yr bonds of HUF 5bln on May 8.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction five billion forint worth of the seven-year government bonds of 2004/F series on May 8, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Monday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest    18 March, 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 March, 2004</p>
<p>    Bonds on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	   103.58 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last</p>
<p>	 auction (April 10)     103.08 pct</p>
<p>NOTE -  The bond bears a floating interest, calculated every half year, adding three percent to year-on-year consumer inflation. The interest is paid once a year, on March 12. The starting interest is 21.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
